    # Index 0 - Jan 1 - New Year / New Beginnings
    {"verse": "Isaiah 43:19", "text": "Behold, I am doing a new thing; now it springs forth, do you not perceive it? I will make a way in the wilderness and rivers in the desert.", "reflection": "A new year is an invitation to trust God with fresh faith. He is not limited by our past failures or yesterday's struggles. Each sunrise is His mercy renewed.", "prayer": "Ask God to open your eyes to the new things He wants to do in your life this year.", "application": "What is one way you can step into this new year with greater trust in God's plans?"},
    # Index 1 - Jan 2
    {"verse": "Lamentations 3:22-23", "text": "The steadfast love of the Lord never ceases; his mercies never come to an end; they are new every morning; great is your faithfulness.", "reflection": "God's faithfulness does not depend on our performance. His mercies are fresh each day, offering grace for every challenge we face. We can begin again because He never stops loving us.", "prayer": "Thank the Lord for His steadfast love that meets you each morning without fail.", "application": "How can you remind yourself of God's fresh mercies when you feel weighed down by yesterday's mistakes?"},
    # Index 2 - Jan 3
    {"verse": "Proverbs 3:5-6", "text": "Trust in the Lord with all your heart, and do not lean on your own understanding. In all your ways acknowledge him, and he will make straight your paths.", "reflection": "Trusting God means releasing our grip on the need to control outcomes. When we acknowledge Him in every decision, He faithfully guides our steps even when the road is unclear.", "prayer": "Pray for the courage to trust God more than your own reasoning today.", "application": "How can you practice acknowledging God in one specific decision you are facing this week?"},
    # Index 3 - Jan 4
    {"verse": "Psalm 46:10", "text": "Be still, and know that I am God. I will be exalted among the nations, I will be exalted in the earth!", "reflection": "In a noisy world, stillness is an act of faith. God invites us to stop striving and rest in the assurance that He is sovereign over all things.", "prayer": "Ask God to quiet your heart and help you rest in His sovereignty today.", "application": "What is one way you can create space for stillness and silence with God this week?"},
    # Index 4 - Jan 5
    {"verse": "Philippians 4:13", "text": "I can do all things through him who strengthens me.", "reflection": "Paul wrote these words from prison, not from a place of worldly success. True strength comes from Christ sustaining us through every circumstance, whether abundance or need.", "prayer": "Ask God to be your strength in the areas where you feel weakest.", "application": "How can you lean on Christ's strength rather than your own ability in a current challenge?"},
    # Index 5 - Jan 6
    {"verse": "Romans 8:28", "text": "And we know that for those who love God all things work together for good, for those who are called according to his purpose.", "reflection": "God does not promise that all things are good, but that He weaves all things together for our ultimate good. His purposes are redemptive even when our circumstances are painful.", "prayer": "Thank the Lord that He is working all things together for your good, even what you cannot yet understand.", "application": "How can you trust God's bigger picture when a current situation feels confusing or painful?"},
    # Index 6 - Jan 7
    {"verse": "Joshua 1:9", "text": "Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Do not be frightened, and do not be dismayed, for the Lord your God is with you wherever you go.", "reflection": "Courage is not the absence of fear but the presence of God. He commands us to be strong because He promises to be with us in every place and every moment.", "prayer": "Pray for boldness to face your fears, knowing God walks beside you.", "application": "What is one way you can choose courage over fear in a situation you are currently avoiding?"},
    # Index 7 - Jan 8
    {"verse": "Psalm 119:105", "text": "Your word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my path.", "reflection": "God's Word does not always illuminate the entire road ahead, but it gives us enough light for the next step. Faithful obedience means walking in the light we have been given.", "prayer": "Ask God to deepen your love for His Word and give you insight as you read it.", "application": "How can you make daily Scripture reading a more consistent part of your routine?"},
    # Index 8 - Jan 9
    {"verse": "Jeremiah 29:11", "text": "For I know the plans I have for you, declares the Lord, plans for welfare and not for evil, to give you a future and a hope.", "reflection": "God's plans for us are rooted in His good character. Even when we cannot see the future, we can trust the One who holds it. His intentions toward us are always for our flourishing.", "prayer": "Thank God that His plans for you are good, and ask Him to increase your trust in His timing.", "application": "What is one way you can surrender your own timeline to God's greater plan today?"},
    # Index 9 - Jan 10
    {"verse": "Matthew 11:28-30", "text": "Come to me, all who labor and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest. Take my yoke upon you, and learn from me, for I am gentle and lowly in heart, and you will find rest for your souls.", "reflection": "Jesus offers rest not through escape but through relationship. His yoke is light because He carries the weight with us. We find soul-deep peace when we come to Him honestly.", "prayer": "Pray for the humility to bring your burdens to Jesus instead of carrying them alone.", "application": "How can you come to Jesus with a specific burden you have been trying to carry on your own?"},
    # Index 10 - Jan 11
    {"verse": "Psalm 23:1-3", "text": "The Lord is my shepherd; I shall not want. He makes me lie down in green pastures. He leads me beside still waters. He restores my soul.", "reflection": "A shepherd knows each sheep personally. God knows your name, your needs, and your weariness. He leads you to places of restoration when you follow His voice.", "prayer": "Ask the Good Shepherd to restore your soul and lead you to places of peace today.", "application": "What is one way you can follow the Shepherd's leading toward rest and restoration this week?"},
    # Index 11 - Jan 12
