    {"verse": "Isaiah 40:31", "text": "But they who wait for the Lord shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings like eagles; they shall run and not be weary; they shall walk and not faint.", "reflection": "Waiting on God is not passive; it is an active posture of expectant faith. As we wait, He replenishes what the world depletes. His strength meets us in our patient trust.", "prayer": "Pray for patience to wait on God's timing and for renewed strength in your weariness.", "application": "How can you practice waiting on God in an area where you are tempted to rush ahead?"},
    # Index 13 - Jan 14
    {"verse": "Ephesians 2:10", "text": "For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God prepared beforehand, that we should walk in them.", "reflection": "You are God's masterpiece, crafted with intention and purpose. The good works ahead of you were planned by God before you were born. Walk confidently into what He has prepared.", "prayer": "Ask God to reveal the good works He has prepared for you and give you courage to walk in them.", "application": "What is one way you can step into a good work God may be calling you to this week?"},
    # Index 14 - Jan 15 - MLK Day - Justice, Equality, Love
    {"verse": "Micah 6:8", "text": "He has told you, O man, what is good; and what does the Lord require of you but to do justice, and to love kindness, and to walk humbly with your God?", "reflection": "God's call on our lives is beautifully simple: act justly in a world of injustice, show mercy to those who need it, and walk humbly before our Creator. Justice and love are inseparable in God's kingdom.", "prayer": "Pray for eyes to see injustice around you and hands willing to do something about it.", "application": "How can you pursue justice and show kindness to someone who is marginalized or overlooked today?"},
    # Index 15 - Jan 16
    {"verse": "Galatians 3:28", "text": "There is neither Jew nor Greek, there is neither slave nor free, there is no male and female, for you are all one in Christ Jesus.", "reflection": "The gospel dismantles every wall that divides humanity. In Christ, our deepest identity transcends race, status, and gender. We are called to see every person as an equal image-bearer of God.", "prayer": "Ask God to remove any prejudice from your heart and fill you with love for all people.", "application": "How can you actively build bridges across dividing lines in your community this week?"},
    # Index 16 - Jan 17
    {"verse": "Colossians 3:23-24", "text": "Whatever you do, work heartily, as for the Lord and not for men, knowing that from the Lord you will receive the inheritance as your reward. You are serving the Lord Christ.", "reflection": "Every task, no matter how small, can be an act of worship when done for God's glory. Our work has eternal significance when we offer it to Him.", "prayer": "Ask God to transform your attitude toward work and help you see it as service to Him.", "application": "How can you approach your daily tasks today as an offering to God rather than just a duty?"},
    # Index 17 - Jan 18
