    # Index 29 - Jan 30
    {"verse": "Psalm 34:8", "text": "Oh, taste and see that the Lord is good! Blessed is the man who takes refuge in him!", "reflection": "God invites us to experience His goodness personally, not just believe it intellectually. Like tasting good food, knowing God's goodness requires personal encounter.", "prayer": "Ask God to let you taste and experience His goodness in a fresh way today.", "application": "What is one way you can take refuge in God and experience His goodness rather than just reading about it?"},
    # Index 30 - Jan 31
    {"verse": "Philippians 4:6-7", "text": "Do not be anxious about anything, but in everything by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving, let your requests be made known to God. And the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and your minds in Christ Jesus.", "reflection": "The antidote to anxiety is prayerful gratitude. When we bring our concerns to God with thankful hearts, His supernatural peace stands guard over our minds and emotions.", "prayer": "Pray through your worries one by one, offering each to God with a thankful heart.", "application": "How can you replace anxious thoughts with prayer and thanksgiving when worry begins to build today?"},
    # Index 31 - Feb 1
