    # Index 35 - Feb 5
    {"verse": "Psalm 91:1-2", "text": "He who dwells in the shelter of the Most High will abide in the shadow of the Almighty. I will say to the Lord, My refuge and my fortress, my God, in whom I trust.", "reflection": "God is both shelter and fortress. He is the quiet place of rest and the strong tower of protection. We dwell there not by accident but by choosing to make Him our home.", "prayer": "Pray for the awareness that God is your shelter and fortress in every storm.", "application": "What is one way you can dwell more intentionally in God's presence as your place of safety?"},
    # Index 36 - Feb 6
    {"verse": "Galatians 5:22-23", "text": "But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, self-control; against such things there is no law.", "reflection": "Spiritual fruit grows naturally as we remain connected to Christ. It cannot be manufactured through effort alone. As we abide in Him, His character develops in us organically.", "prayer": "Ask the Holy Spirit to grow His fruit in your life, particularly in the areas where you struggle most.", "application": "How can you cooperate with the Holy Spirit today to develop one fruit you feel is lacking in your life?"},
    # Index 37 - Feb 7
    {"verse": "Psalm 103:12", "text": "As far as the east is from the west, so far does he remove our transgressions from us.", "reflection": "God does not keep a record of forgiven sins. When He removes our transgressions, they are gone — infinitely far from us. We need not carry guilt that God has already dismissed.", "prayer": "Thank God for the completeness of His forgiveness and ask Him to free you from lingering guilt.", "application": "How can you accept God's complete forgiveness and stop punishing yourself for sins He has already removed?"},
    # Index 38 - Feb 8
    {"verse": "Proverbs 18:10", "text": "The name of the Lord is a strong tower; the righteous man runs into it and is safe.", "reflection": "In ancient times, a strong tower was the place of last resort in battle. God's name — His character, His power, His faithfulness — is that refuge for us. We run to Him and find safety.", "prayer": "Pray that you would run to God first when trouble comes rather than to lesser sources of comfort.", "application": "What is one way you can run to God as your strong tower instead of relying on other sources of security?"},
    # Index 39 - Feb 9
    {"verse": "John 14:27", "text": "Peace I leave with you; my peace I give to you. Not as the world gives do I give to you. Let not your hearts be troubled, neither let them be afraid.", "reflection": "The peace Jesus offers is fundamentally different from what the world provides. Worldly peace depends on circumstances; Christ's peace persists through them. It is a gift He has already given.", "prayer": "Ask Jesus to flood your heart with His peace that transcends your circumstances.", "application": "How can you receive Christ's peace today in a situation that is causing you anxiety or fear?"},
    # Index 40 - Feb 10
