    # Index 41 - Feb 11
    {"verse": "1 Corinthians 10:13", "text": "No temptation has overtaken you that is not common to man. God is faithful, and he will not let you be tempted beyond your ability, but with the temptation he will also provide the way of escape, that you may be able to endure it.", "reflection": "You are never alone in your temptation, and you are never without a way through it. God faithfully limits what you face and provides an exit route every single time.", "prayer": "Pray for eyes to see the way of escape God provides when temptation comes.", "application": "What is one way you can prepare in advance for a temptation you know you will face this week?"},
    # Index 42 - Feb 12
    {"verse": "Psalm 145:18", "text": "The Lord is near to all who call on him, to all who call on him in truth.", "reflection": "God is not distant or disinterested. He draws near to those who call on Him sincerely. Proximity to God is not earned by perfection but accessed through honest prayer.", "prayer": "Ask God to make you aware of His nearness throughout this day.", "application": "How can you call on God in truth today, being honest about your needs and desires?"},
    # Index 43 - Feb 13
    {"verse": "Romans 15:13", "text": "May the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, so that by the power of the Holy Spirit you may abound in hope.", "reflection": "Hope is not wishful thinking; it is confidence rooted in God's character. As we believe His promises, He fills us with joy and peace that overflow into a life marked by hope.", "prayer": "Pray that the God of hope would fill you with joy, peace, and abundant hope today.", "application": "How can you choose to believe God's promises today in an area where hope feels thin?"},
    # Index 44 - Feb 14
    {"verse": "Psalm 86:15", "text": "But you, O Lord, are a God merciful and gracious, slow to anger and abounding in steadfast love and faithfulness.", "reflection": "God's love is not volatile or conditional. He is slow to anger and overflowing with steadfast love. His faithfulness never wavers regardless of our inconsistency.", "prayer": "Thank God for His patient, unfailing love that never gives up on you.", "application": "How can you reflect God's patient, steadfast love to someone in your life today?"},
    # Index 45 - Feb 14 (Valentine's Day) - God's Love
    {"verse": "1 John 4:16", "text": "So we have come to know and to believe the love that God has for us. God is love, and whoever abides in love abides in God, and God abides in him.", "reflection": "God does not merely show love; He is love. Every expression of genuine love flows from His nature. When we abide in love, we abide in God Himself. His love is the source and standard of all love.", "prayer": "Ask God to root you so deeply in His love that it overflows into every relationship you have.", "application": "How can you abide more deeply in God's love today and let it shape how you love others?"},
    # Index 46 - Feb 15
    {"verse": "1 Corinthians 13:4-5", "text": "Love is patient and kind; love does not envy or boast; it is not arrogant or rude. It does not insist on its own way; it is not irritable or resentful.", "reflection": "True love is defined by action, not just emotion. Patience, kindness, and humility are choices we make daily. This love reflects Christ's character working through us.", "prayer": "Pray for the strength to love patiently and kindly, even when it is difficult.", "application": "What is one way you can practice patience and kindness toward someone who tests your limits?"},
    # Index 47 - Feb 16
    {"verse": "Psalm 63:1", "text": "O God, you are my God; earnestly I seek you; my soul thirsts for you; my flesh faints for you, as in a dry and weary land where there is no water.", "reflection": "Spiritual thirst is a gift. It draws us to the only Source that can truly satisfy. When your soul feels dry, it is God Himself — not just His blessings — that you need.", "prayer": "Ask God to increase your thirst for Him and to satisfy your deepest longings.", "application": "How can you earnestly seek God today rather than settling for lesser sources of satisfaction?"},
    # Index 48 - Feb 17
    {"verse": "Ephesians 4:32", "text": "Be kind to one another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, as God in Christ forgave you.", "reflection": "Forgiveness is not optional for believers; it is the overflow of having been forgiven ourselves. As we remember how much Christ has forgiven us, extending grace to others becomes possible.", "prayer": "Ask God to soften your heart toward someone you need to forgive.", "application": "How can you extend forgiveness today to someone who has hurt you, following Christ's example?"},
    # Index 49 - Feb 18
    {"verse": "Psalm 121:1-2", "text": "I lift up my eyes to the hills. From where does my help come? My help comes from the Lord, who made heaven and earth.", "reflection": "When we look beyond our circumstances to the Creator of all things, perspective shifts. The God who made heaven and earth is not too small for your problems. He is your help.", "prayer": "Pray with confidence that your help comes from the Maker of heaven and earth.", "application": "What is one way you can lift your eyes above your circumstances and look to God for help today?"},
    # Index 50 - Feb 19
    {"verse": "John 15:5", "text": "I am the vine; you are the branches. Whoever abides in me and I in him, he it is that bears much fruit, for apart from me you can do nothing.", "reflection": "Fruitfulness comes from connection, not effort alone. Like a branch drawing life from the vine, we bear fruit by staying connected to Jesus. Apart from Him, our striving produces nothing lasting.", "prayer": "Ask God to help you abide in Christ more deeply and recognize when you are trying to produce fruit in your own strength.", "application": "How can you stay more connected to Jesus throughout your daily activities rather than operating independently?"},
    # Index 51 - Feb 20
    {"verse": "Isaiah 55:8-9", "text": "For my thoughts are not your thoughts, neither are your ways my ways, declares the Lord. For as the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher than your ways and my thoughts than your thoughts.", "reflection": "God's perspective is infinitely higher than ours. When His ways confuse us, it is because we are seeing only a fraction of what He sees. Trust grows as we accept the gap between His wisdom and our understanding.", "prayer": "Pray for humility to accept that God's ways are higher and better than your own.", "application": "How can you trust God's higher perspective when His plan does not match what you expected?"},
    # Index 52 - Feb 21
