    # Index 54 - Feb 23
    {"verse": "James 1:2-3", "text": "Count it all joy, my brothers, when you meet trials of various kinds, for you know that the testing of your faith produces steadfastness.", "reflection": "Joy in trials is not denial of pain; it is confidence in God's purpose. Trials test and strengthen our faith like fire refines gold. The steadfastness produced is worth more than comfort.", "prayer": "Pray for the perspective to see your trials as opportunities for spiritual growth.", "application": "How can you choose joy in a current trial by focusing on the character God is building in you?"},
    # Index 55 - Feb 24
    {"verse": "Psalm 62:1-2", "text": "For God alone my soul waits in silence; from him comes my salvation. He alone is my rock and my salvation, my fortress; I shall not be greatly shaken.", "reflection": "When every other support fails, God alone remains. He is rock, salvation, and fortress all at once. Those who anchor themselves to Him will not be shaken by life's storms.", "prayer": "Ask God to be your solid rock and fortress, the unmovable foundation of your life.", "application": "What is one way you can anchor your soul in God alone rather than relying on other sources of stability?"},
