    # Index 59 - Feb 28/Mar 1
    {"verse": "Hebrews 4:16", "text": "Let us then with confidence draw near to the throne of grace, that we may receive mercy and find grace to help in time of need.", "reflection": "We do not approach God timidly or with shame. Because of Christ, we can come boldly to His throne and find exactly what we need: mercy for our failures and grace for our challenges.", "prayer": "Pray with boldness today, drawing near to God's throne of grace with confidence.", "application": "How can you approach God with greater confidence today, knowing He welcomes you with mercy and grace?"},
    # Index 60 - Mar 1
    {"verse": "Psalm 100:4-5", "text": "Enter his gates with thanksgiving, and his courts with praise! Give thanks to him; bless his name! For the Lord is good; his steadfast love endures forever, and his faithfulness to all generations.", "reflection": "Gratitude is the gateway to God's presence. When we enter with thankfulness and praise, our perspective shifts from what we lack to who God is. His goodness endures forever.", "prayer": "Thank God for three specific blessings in your life and let praise fill your heart.", "application": "How can you make gratitude your first response today rather than complaint or anxiety?"},
    # Index 61 - Mar 2
