    # Index 66 - Mar 7
    {"verse": "Psalm 73:25-26", "text": "Whom have I in heaven but you? And there is nothing on earth that I desire besides you. My flesh and my heart may fail, but God is the strength of my heart and my portion forever.", "reflection": "When everything else fades, God remains. He is not just our helper; He is our portion — our inheritance, our satisfaction, our everything. Even when strength fails, He does not.", "prayer": "Pray that God would truly be your greatest desire above all earthly things.", "application": "What is one way you can choose God as your portion today over something else competing for your heart?"},
