    # Index 80 - Mar 21 - Lent/Easter Season begins
    {"verse": "Isaiah 53:5", "text": "But he was pierced for our transgressions; he was crushed for our iniquities; upon him was the chastisement that brought us peace, and with his wounds we are healed.", "reflection": "The cross was not an accident but an act of deliberate love. Jesus bore our punishment willingly so we could be made whole. Every wound He suffered purchased our healing and peace.", "prayer": "Thank Jesus for the wounds He bore on your behalf and the peace His sacrifice purchased.", "application": "How can you live today with deeper gratitude for the price Christ paid for your freedom?"},
    # Index 81 - Mar 22
    {"verse": "Psalm 22:1", "text": "My God, my God, why have you forsaken me? Why are you so far from saving me, from the words of my groaning?", "reflection": "David's cry became Jesus' cry on the cross. God does not condemn us for feeling forsaken; He entered into that feeling Himself. Jesus knows the anguish of feeling alone so that we never truly are.", "prayer": "Pray honestly about any feelings of God's distance, knowing Jesus understands them completely.", "application": "How can you bring your feelings of spiritual dryness honestly to God rather than hiding them?"},
    # Index 82 - Mar 23
