    # Index 83 - Mar 24
    {"verse": "John 12:24", "text": "Truly, truly, I say to you, unless a grain of wheat falls into the earth and dies, it remains alone; but if it dies, it bears much fruit.", "reflection": "Death precedes resurrection. Jesus taught that fruitfulness requires dying to self. Our greatest growth often comes through seasons of surrender and sacrifice.", "prayer": "Pray for willingness to die to self so that God can bring new life and fruitfulness through you.", "application": "What is one way you can die to a selfish desire today so that something greater can grow?"},
    # Index 84 - Mar 25
    {"verse": "Philippians 2:8", "text": "And being found in human form, he humbled himself by becoming obedient to the point of death, even death on a cross.", "reflection": "The Creator of the universe humbled Himself to the lowest point imaginable. His obedience to the Father took Him to the cross — the ultimate act of love through submission.", "prayer": "Ask God to develop Christ-like humility in your heart and a willingness to obey even when it costs you.", "application": "How can you practice humility and obedience today in a situation that requires laying down your preferences?"},
    # Index 85 - Mar 26
    {"verse": "Matthew 26:39", "text": "And going a little farther he fell on his face and prayed, saying, My Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass from me; nevertheless, not as I will, but as yours.", "reflection": "Even Jesus wrestled in prayer before the cross. Yet He surrendered His will to the Father's. Honest wrestling followed by willing surrender is the deepest form of prayer.", "prayer": "Pray for the courage to say 'not my will but yours' in a difficult area of your life.", "application": "How can you surrender your own desires to God's will in a situation where obedience feels costly?"},
    # Index 86 - Mar 27
    {"verse": "Isaiah 50:6", "text": "I gave my back to those who strike, and my cheeks to those who pull out the beard; I did not hide my face from disgrace and spitting.", "reflection": "The Suffering Servant did not retaliate or withdraw. He faced rejection, pain, and humiliation without turning away. His willingness to suffer reveals the depth of His love for us.", "prayer": "Thank Jesus for not turning away from the suffering that secured your salvation.", "application": "How can you respond to mistreatment with grace and trust in God rather than with retaliation?"},
    # Index 87 - Mar 28
    {"verse": "Luke 23:34", "text": "And Jesus said, Father, forgive them, for they know not what they do.", "reflection": "From the cross, Jesus extended forgiveness to those who crucified Him. This is the heart of the gospel: grace given to the undeserving. If He could forgive from the cross, He can empower us to forgive too.", "prayer": "Ask God to help you forgive as Christ forgave — freely and completely, even when it is not deserved.", "application": "What is one way you can extend forgiveness today to someone who has wronged you?"},
