    # Index 89 - Mar 30
    {"verse": "Matthew 27:51-52", "text": "And behold, the curtain of the temple was torn in two, from top to bottom. And the earth shook, and the rocks were split.", "reflection": "The torn curtain declares that the barrier between God and humanity has been destroyed. Access to God's presence is no longer restricted. Through Christ, we enter freely and boldly.", "prayer": "Thank God that the curtain is torn and you have free access to His presence through Christ.", "application": "How can you boldly enter God's presence today, knowing that nothing separates you from Him?"},
    # Index 90 - Mar 31 - Easter/Resurrection
    {"verse": "Matthew 28:5-6", "text": "But the angel said to the women, Do not be afraid, for I know that you seek Jesus who was crucified. He is not here, for he has risen, as he said. Come, see the place where he lay.", "reflection": "The resurrection changes everything. Death could not hold Him, and it will not hold us. Because Christ is alive, we have living hope, present power, and a future beyond the grave.", "prayer": "Praise the risen Christ and thank Him that His resurrection guarantees your own.", "application": "How can you live today in the power of Christ's resurrection rather than as if He were still in the tomb?"},
    # Index 91 - Apr 1
