    # Index 103 - Apr 13
    {"verse": "Psalm 133:1", "text": "Behold, how good and pleasant it is when brothers dwell together in unity!", "reflection": "Unity among believers is precious in God's sight. It does not mean uniformity but a shared commitment to love despite differences. Christian community at its best reflects the unity of the Trinity.", "prayer": "Pray for unity in your church and among believers you know, especially where there is division.", "application": "How can you promote unity and peace in your faith community this week?"},
    # Index 104 - Apr 14
    {"verse": "Isaiah 30:18", "text": "Therefore the Lord waits to be gracious to you, and therefore he exalts himself to show mercy to you. For the Lord is a God of justice; blessed are all those who wait for him.", "reflection": "God does not withhold grace reluctantly; He waits eagerly to be gracious. He delights in showing mercy. Those who wait for Him find that He has been waiting for them all along.", "prayer": "Thank God that He is eager to be gracious to you and that His mercy is always available.", "application": "How can you receive God's eager grace today rather than trying to earn His favor?"},
    # Index 105 - Apr 15
